  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9955e87d5fb04a39b596e81ebac23d13",
      "statement": "`GET /health` is a passive, never-blocking snapshot: it never contacts a model provider and returns status `ok`, the service version, the configured `openwiki_bin` plus `openwiki_found`, `data_dir`, `store.stats()` as `pool`, and the `describe_model(settings)` block as `model`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/health.py#L17-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00cdecd70f96ce7df0b11685895796c2035b236c99ce2079c121d2b1580a7003:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7e6ffa182d24eeb881917ade1823ae1",
      "statement": "`openwiki_found` is derived by splitting the configured CLI command with `split_command` and testing only its first argv token with `shutil.which`, so a command such as `\"python\" \"fake_openwiki.py\"` is checked as `python`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/health.py#L22-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f0a19bee415000ed5b047591a1b3f7108dc229f2df6ebd28d9c28eb4146f97b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_16323a6f52134ddcaad5359ce792b931",
      "statement": "`GET /health/model` accepts only the `force` query flag, delegates to `app.state.model_cache.check(force=force)`, and maps the probe status to HTTP: `ok` and `unsupported` return 200 while `error` and `not_configured` return 503, always with the same JSON result body.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/routers/health.py#L38-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c5da0da887acb4ce4093ecfe947b660bd53146c94607e3c9599c807fb9ce90cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6900d66614154305b0d84988d17368c3",
      "statement": "Provider configuration is resolved exactly as OpenWiki resolves it: `_parse_env_file` reads `<resolved_config_dir>/.env` with a minimal KEY=VALUE parser (skipping blank lines and `#` comments, stripping a leading `export ` and surrounding quotes, tolerating an unreadable file) and the process environment is layered on top, so the environment wins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/config.py#L145-L148",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c43f749e4454d9dceacb132a5b580b9ccdc4de80ce02a23b895a5a82198ce93:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L103-L125",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97fc4707e21d680eaf4f6881d7125a25245fa10eb60ed08bd33ec1c6fbb0fb84:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6f527a605304470ba8fe41eef3dbd68",
      "statement": "`describe_model` produces a secret-free passive snapshot: provider and `provider_source` (`environment`/`config`/`default`), model and its source, `credential_env` with `credential_present`/`credential_source` (never the value), `base_url` through `redact_url` plus its source, `base_url_warning`/`suggested_base_url`, sorted extra-header names with `extra_headers_error`, `probe_supported`, `note` and `active_check_endpoint`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L128-L197",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b9eb0b79793a2a68acece2514f09b664b743dbd9cddac9fa30bc7981858dda41:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4cbaf0df29994fc5a0e602775a147886",
      "statement": "`PROVIDERS` maps provider ids to frozen `ProviderSpec` records (credential env, base-URL env, default base URL, default model, probe kind, note) and is the single decision table driving both the passive report and the active probe's behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L35-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f316ce1a27503c816985026ca355188d6af1940c9cb2b0e669329226295622a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_045c9e5919404f7894b7ccef535efb01",
      "statement": "A spec with `probe=None` is never probed: the check returns `unsupported` with the spec's `note` as `detail`, which is how providers whose auth is not a plain API key (`bedrock`, `copilot`, `gemini-enterprise`, `openai-chatgpt`) and the unimplemented `nebius` are reported instead of guessed at; an unknown provider id also yields `unsupported` with `unknown provider ...; cannot verify the model`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L428-L435",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:27071097554a9a8210e83c0fc726cca7b0e5177216b2606ebb620b5112975ab9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L66-L75",
