        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb67fc13f49f4f2d9e681254a5d19907",
      "statement": "`ModelStatusCache` memoizes the probe result per app instance and treats an entry as fresh while `time.monotonic() - cached_at < max(MODEL_CHECK_TTL_SECONDS, 0)`, so a TTL of `0` (or a negative value) disables the cache and probes on every call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/config.py#L66-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c75abab6ac9718642eda785796a51704eb5586d79205823527b0a9364920d26f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L384-L412",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6acb8775663b0af71dabe830c8083adaa360b6f042c8f134307d052cae807d21:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_172216274e8e4048a3ed03ff347761c0",
      "statement": "`ModelStatusCache.check` uses double-checked locking: it reads the cache before and again inside an `asyncio.Lock`, so a burst of concurrent requests triggers at most one provider call, `force=true` bypasses a fresh entry but still serializes and refreshes it, and every response carries `cached` to show which path was taken.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L393-L404",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:91101b569d626ff2a01a9d4d0d7636419d90e0e7332ef89537ea05c6dd96279b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_model_status.py#L102-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61b7a3f5846f75010e59d905f5b68cf1cdc1277626cd9fd51b8bff2d75b78abb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_119f39a1f2ab4d72bc9cc544c4878dea",
      "statement": "`_run` evaluates conditions in a fixed order: unknown provider and missing probe kind first (`unsupported`), then the base-URL warning branch, then the `not_configured` checks, so a base URL that includes an endpoint path is diagnosed even when a credential is also missing; the `not_configured` details name the exact missing variable (`<CREDENTIAL_ENV> is not set`, `OPENWIKI_MODEL_ID is not set ...`, or `<BASE_URL_ENV> is not set` only for providers whose base-URL variable has no default).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L436-L489",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4cc842abb33e41b4f01c5b11b5e077e9fae5772c24ba0f73bba2d0f47b6c50ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_model_status.py#L158-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5719bdba3988fce65a704b0a13883e1080ad1e11a9b549d6a3893b5dc398548b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e397f5c19d394e80814079f452e6c87f",
      "statement": "`_probe_once` dispatches by probe kind and always sends `PROBE_PROMPT` as the smallest possible completion: `openai-responses` POSTs `/responses` with a Bearer token, `anthropic` POSTs `/v1/messages` with `x-api-key` and `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`, `gemini` POSTs `/v1beta/models/{model}:generateContent` with the key as a query parameter (stripping a `models/` prefix), and `chat` POSTs `/chat/completions` with a Bearer token; any other probe value raises `ProbeError`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L291-L381",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ff7a8dd07a4edadc3a106fee9f7dd80938cd0e5cc723707b98843d20760dce1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_model_status.py#L193-L210",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4a858380ea81cd20ed33f32761927652a11efdfc4ded15d57032fb8ff6cc13ad:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_04b2a240f40f4866b3565f95b163a332",
      "statement": "Probe failures have distinct, redacted semantics: `httpx.TimeoutException` becomes `error` with `model did not answer within <MODEL_CHECK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS>s`, other `httpx.HTTPError` become `HTTP error: ...`, a successful status with no extractable text becomes `error` with `provider returned an empty completion (streaming-only gateway?)`, and `ProbeError`/`HTTPError` text passes through `redact_text(..., (credential,))` while the reported `endpoint` passes through `redact_url`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L491-L526",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:474087cedb69e0d36c7eaccc7d9a76e6e30d2daa4b05ee50eb1ff6aca4a5b02d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_model_status.py#L129-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3915633cedfe299a05a3627a9f19beff1ce8d08412670724ed430f7a5388e8bc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b79400a5e43d43e98b3c69fdff39e9de",
      "statement": "`_split_base_url` strips trailing slashes and detects a base URL that wrongly includes one of the endpoint paths `/chat/completions`, `/responses`, `/completions` or `/messages`, which `describe_model` reports as `base_url_warning` plus `suggested_base_url` on the passive `model` block without any provider call.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/model_status.py#L153-L163",
